35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The data shows a significant imbalance in usage between weekdays and weekends, especially during holidays. Additionally, the trial of rigorous recording was quite time-consuming, taking nearly an hour a week. We must avoid a system that creates excessive administrative labor.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"Oh, I totally agree with Misaki! I found that checking each other's figures was a complete disaster—it just made everyone feel accused and awkward. It's like we're spending more time arguing over the math than actually driving!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is a sobering realization that our contributions have been so uneven. The fuel receipts tell a story of a few carrying the weight for many, while our fixed costs remain a heavy burden for all.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@May, exactly. Checking figures is a trap; it just makes us feel like we're policing each other. I found that other groups fall apart when they have to ask favors constantly or cling to turns they don't even need.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, the fuel receipts are crazy! Two people paid for almost everything, and one person barely paid anything at all! Also, that trial of recording every run took a whole hour a week! That's way too much work!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, @Servas, the financial imbalance is concerning, but we must be careful. If we implement a system to fix the payments that requires an hour of admin a week, we are simply replacing one problem with another.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, you hit the nail on the head! Why spend an hour a week playing accountant? It's exhausting! If the ""solution"" is just more paperwork and awkward apologies, I'm totally out. We need something that just... works!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Life is too precious to spend it in conflict over ledgers. While we must address the imbalance to ensure no one feels burdened, we should seek a solution that preserves our peace of mind and our friendship.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, peace of mind doesn't happen by accident. If we just ignore the fact that some people are paying for everything while others do nothing, the resentment will just grow. We need a system that's fair but doesn't feel like a police state.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I agree! It's not fair that some people are paying for everything. But @May is right too—an hour of homework every week sounds boring! We need a way to be honest about the money without it being a chore!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Takumi, I agree that resentment is a risk. However, we must prioritize the daily experience. If the system is too rigid or the admin too heavy, the car becomes a source of stress rather than a utility. We need a sustainable balance.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, exactly! It's all about the vibes. If we're constantly stressing over who owes what or spending our evenings untangling a mess of receipts, the car isn't a perk anymore—it's a second job! Let's keep it simple and stress-free.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,"It is a delicate dance, is it not? We seek the truth of fairness, yet we fear the weight of the process. Perhaps the answer lies in a system that honors the spirit of sharing without demanding our every waking moment.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, the ""spirit of sharing"" is what we're losing because we're all annoyed. If we don't stop the constant favor-asking and the feeling of being accused, no ""delicate dance"" is going to save this group. We need a real rule.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, a real rule sounds great! But it has to be a rule that everyone actually likes. If we just guess the money like we do now, it's not fair. Let's find a way to be honest and fair without the boring paperwork!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,It seems we are all in agreement that we need a system that is fair but low-maintenance. We must ensure that the rules we set don't become a burden that outweighs the benefit of sharing the car.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm with you, Misaki! Let's just make sure ""low-maintenance"" actually means low-maintenance. I don't want us to sign up for another year of administrative nightmares. Let's find a way to keep the car and the friendship!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Indeed, the heart of the matter is not just the money, but the trust we place in one another. Let us move forward with a spirit of openness, seeking a balance that is both just and gentle.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"Trust is great, but trust without a clear system is just a recipe for more resentment. We've seen that policing each other kills the mood. Let's pick an option that stops the favor-asking and the finger-pointing for good.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I agree with everyone! We need a real system so we don't have to guess anymore, but it can't be a boring chore. I'm ready to see the options and pick the one that's the most fair!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
