60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Looking at the options, Option C is a recipe for the same administrative burden we just discussed. Recording every distance and dividing costs accordingly would likely take that hour a week we want to avoid.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"@Misaki, you're so right! Option C sounds like a total nightmare. We'd be right back to that ""accountant"" phase where we're all stressing over every single kilometer. No thank you! I want my evenings back!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option C seeks a precision that may cost us our peace. While it is the most mathematically just, we must ask if the cost of our time and tranquility is a price we are willing to pay.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Option C is a disaster. It's exactly the kind of policing that makes people feel accused. If we're constantly tracking every kilometer, we're just inviting more finger-pointing and resentment. I'm against it.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I agree with everyone! Option C sounds like that boring homework we all hated. If we have to record every single trip, it'll just be a chore and we'll probably forget to do it anyway!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"Option A provides the most stability. By having fixed days, we eliminate the need for constant coordination and the stress of not knowing if the car is available or ready for use on a weekday morning.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"Option A sounds like a dream! No more endless group chats trying to coordinate who gets the car when. You just know it's your day, and you're good to go. It's the ultimate low-maintenance vibe!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"Option A offers a quiet simplicity. By accepting a fixed share, we move away from the tension of counting pennies and return to the comfort of a shared bond, where the spirit of the group outweighs the ledger.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, simplicity is good, but Option A has a flaw. If someone clings to a day they don't need, or if we're still asking favors to swap days, we're right back where we started. It has to be a clean break.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I get that! But if we have fixed days, we don't have to guess who's using it anymore! It's like having your own special day with the car. That sounds way more fun and fair!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Takumi, the risk of swapping is smaller than the daily stress of uncertainty. Option A ensures the car is where it should be when you need it. It prioritizes the actual experience of using the vehicle over nominal fairness.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"@Takumi, let's be real—a few swaps here and there are way better than a nightly battle of ""who owes what."" Option A just deletes the admin stress. I'm voting for the one that lets us actually relax!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Takumi, your caution is a gift, for it reminds us to be mindful. Yet, if we strive for a perfection that leaves no room for human flexibility, we may find ourselves in a cold house. Let us choose the path of peace.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, peace isn't just about being flexible; it's about not feeling resentful. Option B is even worse—it just makes one person the boss and everyone else a beggar. Option A is the only one that actually stops the policing. I'm in.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I agree! Option B sounds like it would be awkward to always ask one person for permission. Option A is the best because it's simple, fair, and we can stop guessing about the money! I vote for Option A!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Option A is the only choice that guarantees a predictable daily routine and eliminates the administrative burden. It is the most sustainable and logical solution for our group. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,I'm totally with you all! Option A is the only one that doesn't feel like a part-time job. Let's stop the math wars and just enjoy the ride! I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a joy to see us reach this consensus. By choosing simplicity over scrutiny, we protect our friendship from the coldness of the ledger. I believe this path will bring us lasting harmony. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Takumi,,I've thought it through. Option A is the only way to stop the finger-pointing and the constant favor-asking that kills groups like ours. It's a clean break from the policing. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm so happy we all agree! Option A is the best because it's fair, easy, and we can finally stop guessing about the money. Let's make it work! I vote for Option A!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
